# Line endings — the checkout must match what the tests assert.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default. Without this file every
# Windows clone lands a CRLF worktree while the index is LF, and the source-regex tests in
# test/ (which match hardcoded \n, e.g. test/checkpoint-default-on.test.js) fail on files
# they were never meant to read. `npm run test:fast` — THE merge gate — died at step 56/683
# on a clean Windows clone. CI only runs the gate on ubuntu-latest, so nothing caught it.
#
# Normalize to LF in the repo AND in the worktree, on every platform. Node, PowerShell 5.1,
# Tauri and the sidecar all read LF fine on Windows; the tests do not read CRLF fine anywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched by eol conversion. `text=auto` already detects these, but
# stating them keeps a stray heuristic miss from corrupting a sprite sheet or an installer.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.opus  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.dmg   binary
*.node  binary
*.onnx  binary
*.wasm  binary
